    "result_text": "Done. There's a single test class, and the full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level tenure rule. The level is derived in `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipLevel`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added a fourth factor: `+1` when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 days \u2014 computed as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`.\n- Raised the cap from `3` to `4`.\n- Added `java.time.LocalDate` and `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` imports; updated the Javadoc.\n\nBecause a newly created owner has zero tenure, the tenure factor never fires on creation, so a new owner with an email (`+1`) and `namesakeCount` of 0 (`+1`) tops out at level 3 \u2014 never 4. Only an owner registered more than a year ago can reach level 4. The 3-member household in the spec example doesn't affect the formula (household count isn't a level factor), so that owner is level 3 as required.\n\n**Spec doc** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`): updated the `membershipLevel` description, bumped `maximum` from 3 to 4, and documented the tenure factor.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` passes \u2014 the audit log confirms the newly created owner is recorded at `membershipLevel=3`.",
